<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Required by the bundled mullion-bridge-worker sidecar (a Node.js Single
    Executable Application). Without this, V8's Isolate::Init fails to
    mmap(MAP_JIT) its JS code range under macOS's Hardened Runtime, and the
    worker crashes at startup with:

      # Fatal process out of memory: Failed to reserve virtual memory for CodeRange

    despite the wording, that's not a heap-size problem, it's V8 being
    denied executable memory. Node's own upstream macOS binary ships with
    this same entitlement (nodejs/node tools/osx-entitlements.plist).

    Applies to the whole app bundle, not just the sidecar, since Tauri signs
    all nested binaries with this one file. Harmless for the main WebView
    binary. Deliberately NOT copying Node's other entitlements
    (get-task-allow is debug-only and notarization rejects it;
    disable-executable-page-protection and disable-library-validation are
    unnecessary and notarization-hostile): allow-jit is the one V8
    actually needs.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
